{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 109,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David. Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They encompassed me also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For my love they are my adversaries: but I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "give myself to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his days be few; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let another take his office.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their bread",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also out of their desolate places.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let strangers spoil his labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let there be none to extend mercy to him: neither let there be any to favor his fatherless children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his posterity be cut off; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the generation following let their name be blotted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the LORD; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because that he remembered not to show mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As he loved cursing, so let it come to him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let it be to him as the garment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " covereth him, and for a girdle with which he is girded continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the reward of my adversaries from the LORD, and of them that speak evil against my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But do thou for me, O GOD the Lord, for thy name's sake: because thy mercy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good, deliver thou me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I became also a reproach to them: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they looked upon me they shook their heads.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Help me, O LORD my God: O save me according to thy mercy:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may know that this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy hand; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou, LORD, hast done it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let my adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will greatly praise the LORD with my mouth; yes, I will praise him among the multitude.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.109.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.109.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he will stand at the right hand of the poor, to save ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from those that condemn his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
